# Secrets & local environment — never commit these
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.pfx
*.p12
secrets/
credentials/
*.local

# Claude Code local, machine-specific settings
.claude/settings.local.json

# Local-only working docs kept out of the published repo (original PRD/design
# notes, internal roadmaps/migration runbooks, WIP handoffs). Retained on disk
# for the author's reference; never published.
scratch/

# Orchestration run-state — local session bookkeeping, not product history.
# Gitignored so the guided loop's single-checkout discard (`git stash -u`) and
# `git add -A` never sweep or commit it, and so it never dirties the tree that
# reconcile inspects (ADR 0009). It persists on local disk across sessions.
.agents/run-state.yaml

# The two files that TRAVEL WITH run-state and must share its treatment exactly
# (ADR 0022, ADR 0019 v3.4): the finding BODIES whose one-line index lives inside
# run-state, and the archived overflow of run-state's `note:`. Both are the cold
# half of a hot/cold split whose hot half is gitignored — so ignoring them is what
# keeps the pair consistent. Ignoring is also what makes them SURVIVE: an untracked
# file is swept by the pause path's `git stash --include-untracked` and shows up in
# the `git status --porcelain` that `reconcile` reads as scratch sitting on the green
# checkpoint (which it then discards). An ignored file is invisible to both, exactly
# like run-state.yaml. Same-machine, same as run-state.
.agents/findings/
.agents/run-state-note-archive.md

# The last-known-good copy `write` takes before replacing run-state. It exists
# because run-state is gitignored: a botched upstream transform in a pipe used to
# destroy it permanently, with no `git restore` to fall back on. Recovery beats
# detection here — classifying every valid and invalid document correctly, forever,
# is not a thing we can do, but keeping the previous copy needs no classification.
# It MUST be ignored for the reason the block above spells out: an untracked file is
# swept by the pause path's stash and discarded by reconcile as scratch, so an
# unignored backup would be destroyed by the very recovery path it serves.
.agents/run-state-prev.yaml

# Orchestration run-metrics — the event spine + assembled run packets (ADR 0019
# Tier 1). Local run bookkeeping, NOT product history; gitignored for the same
# ADR 0009 reasons as run-state (the loop's `git add -A` / `git stash -u` must
# never sweep or commit it, and it must not dirty the tree reconcile inspects).
# The assembled run-metrics.json is a portable single file — archive a run by
# copying it out, not by committing this live directory. Also covers
# .agents/metrics/driver-mode/<session>.jsonl (thin-loop-driver T3).
.agents/metrics/
.agents/metrics*

# The loop driver's own run directories (thin-loop-driver T3/T7): the
# session-keyed driver-mode mark (.agents/driver-mode/<session-id>, cleared on
# its own session's SessionStart startup/resume) and .agents/loop/<run_id>/
# (handoff files, script-written result files, the routing log — T7/T8/T9).
# Local run bookkeeping, NOT product history; same ADR 0009 reasons as
# run-state.yaml above, including that an UNignored entry here would be swept
# by the pause path's `git stash --include-untracked` and read by `reconcile`
# in `git status --porcelain` as scratch sitting on the green checkpoint.
.agents/driver-mode/
.agents/loop/

# gspec build run-state — transient driver bookkeeping, not product history.
# The adapter reads `.gspec/build/status.json` for the two-drivers interlock
# (ADR 0020 D5) and does so FAIL-SOFT, so its absence is a supported state and
# ignoring it costs nothing. `.gspec/config.json` is NOT ignored: it records the
# install target and is the only in-repo trace that gspec is wired up here.
.gspec/build/

# gspec agent-run logs — per-run validator/QA feedback, rewritten on every agent
# run. Same category as `.gspec/build/` above, plus one reason of its own: each
# entry's `SPEC:` line carries an ABSOLUTE local path (`/Users/<name>/...`), so
# committing it would publish one machine's directory layout from a repo whose
# whole point is being portable. Nothing reads it programmatically — it is human
# review output, and it regenerates.
.gspec/agent-runs/

